WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.994
Lab 2 runs in a worldwide or G C C test
tenant, with a test management group,

2
00:00:04.994 --> 00:00:10.775
subscription and resource group, never
production, and fictional users and groups.

3
00:00:10.775 --> 00:00:17.150
Eligible users need Microsoft Entra I
D P2 or Microsoft Entra I D Governance.

4
00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:20.030
You prepare an app with
Reader on each test scope,

5
00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:22.838
and write the desired
state for the test scopes.

6
00:00:22.838 --> 00:00:26.593
You plan live, then apply under
a User Access Administrator

7
00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:30.974
assignment that lasts one day, and
try the narrower role on one scope.

8
00:00:30.974 --> 00:00:33.225
No Graph permission is needed at all.

9
00:00:33.225 --> 00:00:37.297
The back-out waits at least five
minutes after the last assignment,

10
00:00:37.297 --> 00:00:40.407
removes the eligible
assignments the run created,

11
00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:43.443
restores each policy from
the dry run's state file,

12
00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:47.737
removes the app's roles and the app,
and deletes the test output folders.

13
00:00:47.737 --> 00:00:49.940
The authors haven't run Lab 2.
